## goal
Implement `calc-engine` only: `/proyectos/[id]/resultados.json` contract, RH lookup from `rules/renovacion.json`, people lookup from `tabla_caudal_por_persona`, midpoint range policy, `aprox -> min=max=aprox`, `max-of-both` governing logic, area/equipment/project summaries, dual human+structured traces, rounding to 2 decimals, and integration using `proyectos/1/input.json`.

## assumptions
- Source of truth = `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-calc-engine-design.md`.
- Existing `proyectos/1/input.json` is valid seed fixture and stays read-only for calc engine except generated `resultados.json`.
- `catalog_type` in input is already canonical from input-pipeline, so calc engine can do exact lookup against `rules/renovacion.json`.
- Repo pattern for Python tooling should mirror `lib/input-pipeline/` with pure functions plus thin filesystem integration.
- No `pdd/calc-engine/explore` or `requirements` artifacts exist yet; plan grounded on spec + repo evidence.

## constraints
- Exclude spec selection, market equipment sizing, memory generation, and any `spec.json` work.
- Exclude advanced equipment optimization; v1 only aggregates final area demand onto existing `equipment[].serves_area_ids` / `areas[].equipment_ids` links.
- Keep governing policy fixed to `max-of-both`; no configurable policy layer.
- Store rounded values at 2 decimals; traces must match stored rounded outputs.
- Support human + structured traces for both applicable and non-applicable methods.
- Fail/block explicitly on unresolvable RH lookup; people lookup missing row should follow spec behavior, not invent fallback sizing.

## impacted areas
- `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-22-calc-engine-design.md`
- `.pi/agents/renovacion-agent/calculator-dev-agent.md`
- `.pi/agents/renovacion-agent/calculator-agent.md`
- `rules/renovacion.json`
- `proyectos/1/input.json`
